{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.MassIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.MassIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.cycleMassTrace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.cycleMassTrace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L142-L153","doc":"`cycleMassTrace` equals `∫_A(u · hol w · c)` where `c = μ ∘ coev` is the Casimir element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.cycleMassTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.cycleMassTrace","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L134-L140","doc":"**Categorical trace of the left-multiplication mass endomorphism of `hol w`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.cycleFrobeniusEval_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.cycleFrobeniusEval_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L124-L132","doc":"`cycleFrobeniusEval` equals `∫_A(u · hol w)` where `u = Ψ ∘ η` is the density. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.cycleFrobeniusEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.cycleFrobeniusEval","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L115-L122","doc":"**Frobenius evaluation of the non-abelian holonomy of a transport word (Option 1).**\nForms the ordered convolution product `hol fh w : 𝟙_ C ⟶ fh.obj` first, then applies\nthe mass integrand `Ψ` and the Frobenius form `∫_A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.massComposite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.massComposite","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**Categorical mass morphism**: the composite `(λ ⊗ id) ∘ Δ`\nin the monoidal category `C`, whose composition with a cycle `ϱ : 𝟙 → A`\nand the Frobenius form `∫_A` gives the pre-norm mass scalar.\n\nThis uses the canonical `FrobeniusHopfData` from quantum-universe.lean\nto maintain type consistency with the foundational definitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.scalarMass_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.scalarMass_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L99-L102","doc":"Scalar mass is non-negative (immediate from norm). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.scalarMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.scalarMass","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L82-L97","doc":"**Scalar mass** — the post-τ Archimedean realisation of\n`frobeniusMass`.  Requires the Archimedean norm structure\n`[NormedCommRing R]`; lives downstream of the formal chain.\n\nGiven the image `x : R` of the categorical trace under the fibre\nfunctor, `scalarMass x = ‖x‖`.  This corresponds to evaluating\nthe categorical Frobenius norm at the substrate parameter\n`q = q₀ ∈ ℝ`.\n\nPer `QOU.GroundRingAnnotations`, this declaration is **not**\npart of the formal pre-Arch chain — it is the Archimedean\nbridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.frobeniusMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.frobeniusMass","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.lean#L66-L80","doc":"**Frobenius mass** — the mass formula evaluated in the ground ring\n`R` via the Frobenius pairing.\n\nGiven the image `x : R` of the categorical trace under the fibre\nfunctor, the Frobenius norm `‖x‖_F` is `⟨x, x⟩_F`-derived (a\nquantity in `R`, not in `ℝ`).  The caller supplies the Frobenius\npairing through the `frobenius_form` argument.\n\nFor the Archimedean evaluation of `‖·‖_F` at `q = q₀`, see\n`scalarMass` below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}